/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Sustainable Smart Water Filling System Using Sensor-Based Automation )
/E (Sustainable Smart Water Filling System Using Sensor-Based Automation )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (is an innovative and eco-friendly solution designed to optimize water usage, energy  consumption, and user convenience through intelligent automation. The system  integrates a combination of sensors, actuators, and control modules to automatically  manage water filling, heating, and monitoring processes without manual intervention.  An ultrasonic sensor continuously monitors the water level to prevent overflow and dry  running of the pump, while a temperature sensor ensures precise control over the water  heating process. The microcontroller acts as the central control unit, processing real- time sensor data and operating relays to automate the pump and heater. A GSM module  enables instant communication by sending alerts to the user in case of abnormal  conditions such as low water levels or overheating. In addition, motor drivers facilitate  mechanical operations, and status indicators provide visual feedback for ease of  monitoring.  The entire system is powered through an SMPS and buck converter setup, ensuring  stable voltage regulation and energy efficiency. Designed with reliability,  sustainability, and affordability in mind, the system is suitable for residential,  commercial, and small-scale industrial applications. By integrating automation and  intelligent control, this smart water management solution minimizes resource wastage,  promotes energy conservation, and contributes to the broader goal of sustainable living. )
/E (is an innovative and eco-friendly solution designed to optimize water usage, energy  consumption, and user convenience through intelligent automation. The system  integrates a combination of sensors, actuators, and control modules to automatically  manage water filling, heating, and monitoring processes without manual intervention.  An ultrasonic sensor continuously monitors the water level to prevent overflow and dry  running of the pump, while a temperature sensor ensures precise control over the water  heating process. The microcontroller acts as the central control unit, processing real- time sensor data and operating relays to automate the pump and heater. A GSM module  enables instant communication by sending alerts to the user in case of abnormal  conditions such as low water levels or overheating. In addition, motor drivers facilitate  mechanical operations, and status indicators provide visual feedback for ease of  monitoring.  The entire system is powered through an SMPS and buck converter setup, ensuring  stable voltage regulation and energy efficiency. Designed with reliability,  sustainability, and affordability in mind, the system is suitable for residential,  commercial, and small-scale industrial applications. By integrating automation and  intelligent control, this smart water management solution minimizes resource wastage,  promotes energy conservation, and contributes to the broader goal of sustainable living. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
