451 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (encoders for accurate water level monitoring and refill alerts, ensuring reliability in real-time applications. Similarly, mechanical innovations such as belt drives, telescopic tubes, and cam-based grippers have been explored to achieve precise motion and automation in handling.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
452 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In addition, work on temperature-controlled systems ensures water can be maintained at user-preferred conditions, while electronic design advancements such as switch-mode power supplies \(SMPS\) improve system stability and efficiency. These multidisciplinary contributions demonstrate how automation and mechatronics can transform traditional water dispensing into smart, efficient, and sustainable systems. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
