571 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The ATmega328P is an 8-bit AVR microcontroller widely used in embedded systems and Arduino boards, known for its versatility and low power consumption. It operates at up to 20 MHz, with 32 KB of flash memory, 2 KB of SRAM, and 1 KB of EEPROM. The chip supports 23 GPIO pins, features a 10-bit ADC with six channels, and includes three timers \(two 8 -bit and one 16-bit\) for precise timing and PWM\(Pulse-width modulation\) control. Communication options include UART, SPI, and I2C\(Inter-Integrated Circuit\). With its low power modes and bootloader support, it is ideal for sensor interfaces, robotics, and low-power applications. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [12 13]
>>
endobj
