580 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Motor and Pump Control: Through the L298N motor driver and relays, the Arduino Uno controls DC motors and pumps. PWM\(pulse width modulation\) outputs regulate motor speed, while digital pins manage the relay switching for pump and heater operation.  Decision-Making Logic: Using its programmable flash memory and interrupt  system, the Arduino Uno executes control algorithms to automatically activate the  pump, motor, or heater based on sensor data.  Communication with External Systems: The Arduino Uno works with the GSM800 module using UART. It can send SMS alerts to users about water level or temperature conditions, ensuring reliable remote monitoring. Power Management: With buck converters providing stable 5V supply, the Uno maintains reliable operation. Low-power modes of the ATmega328P can also be leveraged for energy efficiency in extended use. )
/E (Motor and Pump Control: Through the L298N motor driver and relays, the Arduino Uno controls DC motors and pumps. PWM\(pulse width modulation\) outputs regulate motor speed, while digital pins manage the relay switching for pump and heater operation.  Decision-Making Logic: Using its programmable flash memory and interrupt  system, the Arduino Uno executes control algorithms to automatically activate the  pump, motor, or heater based on sensor data.  Communication with External Systems: The Arduino Uno works with the GSM800 module using UART. It can send SMS alerts to users about water level or temperature conditions, ensuring reliable remote monitoring. Power Management: With buck converters providing stable 5V supply, the Uno maintains reliable operation. Low-power modes of the ATmega328P can also be leveraged for energy efficiency in extended use. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
581 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Override Control: The microcontroller can also provide a manual override function, where users can manually operate the roof using switches, buttons, or remote control, with the ATmega328P handling user input via its GPIO\(General purpose input/output\) pins.  In this project, the Arduino Uno plays a central role in processing sensor data,  controlling actuators, and enabling communication, making the mini project an  efficient and automated water and temperature management system. )
/E (Override Control: The microcontroller can also provide a manual override function, where users can manually operate the roof using switches, buttons, or remote control, with the ATmega328P handling user input via its GPIO\(General purpose input/output\) pins.  In this project, the Arduino Uno plays a central role in processing sensor data,  controlling actuators, and enabling communication, making the mini project an  efficient and automated water and temperature management system. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
