/S /P
/E (Ultrasonic sensors are key components in automation systems, offering non-contact, fast, and accurate distance or level measurements. They work by emitting sound pulses and measuring the time it takes for the echo to return, allowing precise calculation of the distance to an object. In the smart water filling system, these sensors reliably monitor water levels and trigger actions such as operating motors, pumps, or relays based on set thresholds. Their use enhances accuracy, safety, and real-time control, making the system more efficient and convenient.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
